<xri version="1.0">
   <description>
      <p>Benny Colyn&apos;s PixInsight Scripts</p>
   </description>
   <platform os="all" arch="noarch" version="1.8.8:1.9.9">
      <package fileName="bcolyn-scripts-20261110203258.zip" sha1="e1a4172304f0813375b917101b8d9e26280ff175" type="script" releaseDate="20261110">
         <title>Benny Colyn&apos;s PixInsight Scripts v2026.11.10</title>
         <description>
            <p>Utilities &gt; 3-way Compare: Tiles up to three selected image windows side-by-side horizontally, each filling one column at full workspace height. Nice when comparing A,B and a ground truth image. Especially useful for ultrawide monitors.</p>
            <p>Mask &gt; Annotation To Mask: Builds a protection mask from an annotations SVG created by AnnotateImage (Script &gt; Render &gt; AnnotateImage, Output Mode = &quot;Generate SVG overlay&quot;). Useful for quickly building a mask that protects most of the small (PGC etc) galaxies in an image. Requires PixInsight 1.9.4 &quot;Lockhart&quot; or later.</p>
            <p>Render &gt; Aster: A V8-runtime PJSR port of Aster (originally for Siril/sirilpy), for adding a soft glow and optional diffraction spikes to a stretched, stars-only image. Supports Newtonian (4-arm) and JWST-style (6+2-arm) spike patterns, spectral (rainbow) diffraction tinting, and exclusion masks for glow and spikes independently. Requires PixInsight 1.9.4 &quot;Lockhart&quot; or later. Licensed under the GNU General Public License v3.0 or later; the license text is bundled as LICENSE-GPL-3.0.txt next to the script.</p>
            <p>Utilities &gt; Export For Archival: Exports all currently open images as compressed XISF files to a chosen directory, and saves their full processing history as a .xpsm process container file and a human-readable .log summary.</p>
            <p>Utilities &gt; Fetch HiPS Reference: Downloads a reference image cutout from a CDS HiPS survey (DSS2, SDSS9, PanSTARRS, in colour or single band) matching the astrometric solution of an open, plate-solved image, using the hips2fits service. The cutout is requested at the source image&apos;s dimensions, field of view and rotation -- mirrored solutions included -- so it can be blinked against the original to check whether faint structure is real. A blank result is not an error: it means the chosen survey has no coverage at those coordinates. FITS cutouts of the 16-bit single-band surveys can optionally be rescaled to [0,1], since they otherwise open as a flat grey. Requires PixInsight 1.9.4 &quot;Lockhart&quot; or later and an image with an astrometric solution.</p>
         </description>
      </package>
   </platform>
</xri>
